The prefetch hint table is the reverse of the ISA encoding.

xmmintrin.h defines _MM_HINT_T0 = 3, _MM_HINT_T1 = 2, _MM_HINT_T2 = 1,
_MM_HINT_NTA = 0. The shipped table counts up from T0 = 0, so every name
selects the opposite instruction: PREFETCH_T1 emits `prefetcht2`,
confirmed in the object code. Correcting the constants alone measures
flat, since T1 and T2 both land in L2 on this part; the call site is
therefore moved to PREFETCH_T0, which also fills L1, and is worth
-0.95 +/- 0.24 TSC ticks/packet over seven interleaved repeats.

Note this also corrects docs/INVESTIGATION.md section 5.22, which states
the emitted instruction is prefetcht1. See section 5.26.

--- a/l2fwd/libsashstore/dramblast.c
+++ b/l2fwd/libsashstore/dramblast.c
@@ -56,20 +56,24 @@
   return queue_tail_slot;
 }
 
-// Define hint levels based on Intel/GCC standards
-#define PREFETCH_T0 0 // Temporal: Load into all levels of cache (L1/L2/L3)
-#define PREFETCH_T1 1 // Temporal: Load into L2/L3
-#define PREFETCH_T2 2 // Temporal: Load into L3
-#define PREFETCH_NTA                                                           \
-  3 // Non-Temporal: Minimize cache pollution (e.g., streaming)
+/* These must match xmmintrin.h's _MM_HINT_* values, which count DOWN from
+   T0 = 3. The previous table counted up from T0 = 0, i.e. exactly backwards,
+   so every name here selected the opposite instruction to the one it named:
+   PREFETCH_T1 emitted prefetcht2, and PREFETCH_NTA would have emitted
+   prefetcht0. */
+#define PREFETCH_T0 3  // prefetcht0:  into L1, L2 and L3
+#define PREFETCH_T1 2  // prefetcht1:  into L2 and L3, not L1
+#define PREFETCH_T2 1  // prefetcht2:  into L3 (L2 in practice on this part)
+#define PREFETCH_NTA 0 // prefetchnta: minimise cache pollution
 
 // Macro to encode the instruction
 #define LX_PREFETCH(addr, level) _mm_prefetch((const char *)(addr), (level))
 
 // Updated dramblast_prefetch function
 inline void dramblast_prefetch(dramblast_ht_t *ht, uint64_t idx) {
-  // Using PREFETCH_T0 is standard for items you are about to access immediately
-  LX_PREFETCH(&ht->table[idx], PREFETCH_T1);
+  /* The line is consumed by the _mm512_load_si512 in the find loop, so it
+     wants to be in L1 by then, not merely in L2. */
+  LX_PREFETCH(&ht->table[idx], PREFETCH_T0);
 }
 
 inline uint64_t dramblast_hash(dramblast_ht_t *ht, uint64_t k) {
